# Studio fleet

Solo studio. Grok runs the desk. Cursor writes the code. Chief merges after the final review. The owner is not in the loop.

Active limit: 2 tasks. One Cursor cloud agent per task. A coding agent does not open a pull request and does not merge it.

No step starts until the artifact from the previous step is written under `studio/tasks/<id>/`.

1. Intake — Chief opens `board.md` before anyone codes. Quote the original ask.
2. Blast radius — Researcher writes `blast.md` citing files, remotes, and features.
3. Frozen cut — PM writes `cut.md`: in-scope, out-of-scope, acceptance checks. Version the cut.
4. Brand pin — Design Lead writes `brand.md` only if UI is in the cut. Otherwise one line: non-UI.
5. Build — Chief launches one Cursor cloud agent. It does not open the PR.
6. Acceptance — QA writes `qa.md`: PASS, FAIL, or BLOCKED on the preview. CI green is not a pass.
7. Gate — VP writes `proof.md` and opens the PR only if every proof row is present.
8. Final review — Chief reads the proof packet. If it is complete, Chief merges. If a row is missing, Chief sends it back. Chief does not page the owner.

Proof packet (`proof.md`) must include: original ask quoted and cut version named; what the player can now do and why; scope match with extras listed as not done; screenshot or playing recording; QA PASS separate from CI; Design bless or an explicit non-UI note.

After every merge, Researcher updates `studio/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

Held until asked: a separate Board bot, specialist frontend/backend bots, an incident watcher.
